{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract analyze comprehensive [-h] [--vcf-inputs VCF_INPUTS [VCF_INPUTS ...]]\n                                        [--skip-calling] [--batch BATCH] [--force]\n                                        [--force-step STEP] [--dry-run] [--help-all]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --vcf-inputs VCF_INPUTS [VCF_INPUTS ...]\n                        One or more input VCF files (e.g., SNV, CNV, SV).\n  --skip-calling        Without --vcf-inputs, don't call variants from --input; run only the\n                        BAM/CRAM metrics and lineage steps.\n  --batch BATCH         Path to a CSV/TSV file for batch processing multiple samples.\n  --help-all            Show this help with the advanced options too, and exit.\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nresuming:\n  Completed steps are recorded in <output>.steps.json and skipped when a rerun's inputs,\n  settings and tools are unchanged.\n\n  --force, --no-resume  Rerun every step, ignoring the steps an earlier run completed.\n  --force-step STEP     Rerun STEP and the steps that use its outputs (repeatable). Steps: info,\n                        mt-haplogroup, y-haplogroup, snp, indel, annotate, discovery.\n  --dry-run             Print which steps would run or be skipped, and why, then exit.\n\n2 advanced options not shown; 'wgsextract analyze comprehensive --help-all' lists them.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract analyze comprehensive --input sample.cram\n  wgsextract analyze comprehensive --input sample.cram --force-step annotate\n  wgsextract analyze comprehensive --vcf-inputs snps.vcf.gz sv.vcf.gz\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  The QC, lineage, variant and annotation outputs of each step, and a summary;\n  analyze.steps.json records the completed steps.\n\nneeds:\n  bcftools, samtools, tabix; hours on a 30x genome.\n",
